      "source": [
        "# Section B: Base CIR Model Implementation & Calibration\n",
        "\n",
        "## Overview\n",
        "We implement the Cox-Ingersoll-Ross (CIR) model to simulate and calibrate the term structure of interest rates.\n",
        "\n",
        "**CIR Process (SDE):**\n",
        "$$dr_t = \\kappa(\\theta - r_t)dt + \\sigma\\sqrt{r_t}dW_t$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where:\n",
        "- $\\kappa$ = mean reversion speed\n",
        "- $\\theta$ = long-term mean level\n",
        "- $\\sigma$ = volatility (standard deviation of the random shock)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Feller Condition:** For positivity, we require $2\\kappa\\theta \\geq \\sigma^2$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Calibration Approach:** Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) with OLS fallback\n",
        "- **MLE**: Statistically rigorous, directly maximizes likelihood of observed data\n",
        "- **OLS**: Robust alternative if MLE fails, regression-based on mean-reverting dynamics\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qsqmmTjRQqvb"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 2.1: CIR Theoretical Framework & Discretization\n",
        "\n",
        "We discretize the CIR process using Euler-Maruyama scheme for calibration."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "jp-MarkdownHeadingCollapsed": true,
        "id": "eyDs01hQQqvb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Breakdown of the Feller Condition and Practical Handling\n",
        "\n",
        "The Feller condition ($2\\kappa\\theta > \\sigma^2$) guarantees that the interest rate process $r_t$ remains strictly positive and never reaches zero.\n",
        "\n",
        "**When it breaks down:**\n",
        "This mathematical condition fails when market volatility ($\\sigma$) spikes disproportionately compared to the long-term mean ($\\theta$) and the mean-reversion speed ($\\kappa$). In practice, this occurs during **Zero-Interest-Rate Policy (ZIRP) environments** or severe macroeconomic crises. When central banks force the target rate near zero, normal levels of volatility will easily exceed $2\\kappa\\theta$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Handling the breakdown:**\n",
        "* **Optimization Penalties:** During Risk-Neutral calibration, the optimizer is strictly constrained to reject any parameter combinations violating the condition by applying a massive penalty error (`if 2 * kappa * theta <= sigma**2: return 1e6`).\n",
        "* **Simulation Bounds & Jump-Diffusion:** In Euler-Maruyama simulations, a programmatic lower bound (`max(r[i], 1e-8)`) is enforced before calculating the square root. Furthermore, introducing a **Jump-Diffusion extension** allows the model to handle massive sudden shocks via a Poisson jump process ($J_t dN_t$) rather than artificially inflating the diffusion parameter ($\\sigma$), naturally protecting the Feller boundary."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 9,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "9zZ45X4MQqvb",
        "outputId": "f451613a-f803-4a7f-99ee-200d164eb2f7"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "CIRModel class defined with simulation and bond pricing methods\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# CIR Model Class for simulation and calibration\n",
        "class CIRModel:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Cox-Ingersoll-Ross interest rate model.\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    def __init__(self, kappa, theta, sigma):\n",
        "        self.kappa = kappa\n",
        "        self.theta = theta\n",
        "        self.sigma = sigma\n",
        "\n",
        "    def check_feller_condition(self):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Verify 2*kappa*theta >= sigma^2 for process positivity.\"\"\"\n",
        "        return 2 * self.kappa * self.theta >= self.sigma ** 2\n",
        "\n",
        "    def simulate_path(self, r0, dt, n_steps, seed=None):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Simulate CIR path using Euler-Maruyama scheme.\"\"\"\n",
        "        if seed is not None:\n",
        "            np.random.seed(seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "        r = np.zeros(n_steps + 1)\n",
        "        r[0] = r0\n",
        "\n",
        "        for i in range(n_steps):\n",
        "            dW = np.random.normal(0, np.sqrt(dt))\n",
        "            # Ensure positivity by taking max with small value\n",
        "            r[i+1] = r[i] + self.kappa * (self.theta - r[i]) * dt + self.sigma * np.sqrt(max(r[i], 1e-8)) * dW\n",
        "            r[i+1] = max(r[i+1], 1e-8)  # Enforce positivity\n",
        "\n",
        "        return r\n",
        "\n",
        "    def bond_price(self, r, T, t=0):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Calculate zero-coupon bond price P(t, T) = B(t, T)^A(t, T) * exp(-A(t, T) * r(t)).\"\"\"\n",
        "        tau = T - t\n",
        "        if tau <= 0:\n",
        "            return 1.0\n",
        "\n",
        "        h = np.sqrt(self.kappa ** 2 + 2 * self.sigma ** 2)\n",
        "        a_term = 2 * h * np.exp((self.kappa + h) * tau / 2)\n",
        "        denom = 2 * h + (self.kappa + h) * (np.exp(h * tau) - 1)\n",
        "        B = 2 * (np.exp(h * tau) - 1) / denom\n",
        "        A = ((2 * self.kappa * self.theta) / (self.sigma ** 2)) * np.log(a_term / denom)\n",
        "\n",
        "        return np.exp(A - B * r)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def yield_to_maturity(self, r, T, t=0):\n",
        "        \"\"\"Calculate yield to maturity (continuously compounded).\"\"\"\n",
        "        P = self.bond_price(r, T, t)\n",
        "        tau = T - t\n",
        "        return -np.log(P) / tau if tau > 0 else 0.0\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"CIRModel class defined with simulation and bond pricing methods\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "jp-MarkdownHeadingCollapsed": true,
        "id": "6tNFw5nXQqvb"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 2.2: Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) Calibration\n",
        "\n",
        "MLE directly optimizes the likelihood function of observed data under the CIR model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "B2wCEic-Qqvb"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from scipy.optimize import minimize\n",
        "\n",
        "def mle_calibration(rates, dt, initial_guess=None, verbose=True):\n",
        "    mean_rate = np.mean(rates)\n",
        "    std_rate = np.std(rates)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if initial_guess is None:\n",
        "        kappa_init = 0.05\n",
        "        theta_init = mean_rate\n",
        "        sigma_init = std_rate * 0.3\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        kappa_init, theta_init, sigma_init = initial_guess\n",
        "\n",
        "    def negative_log_likelihood(params):\n",
        "        kappa, theta, sigma = params\n",
        "\n",
        "        if kappa <= 0 or theta <= 0 or sigma <= 0:\n",
        "            return 1e10\n",
        "\n",
        "        # FELLER CONDITION as HARD constraint: 2κθ >= σ²\n",
        "        # Enforce with 2% safety margin\n",
        "        if 2 * kappa * theta < sigma ** 2 * 1.02:\n",
        "            return 1e10\n",
        "\n",
        "        exp_minus_kappa_dt = np.exp(-kappa * dt)\n",
        "\n",
        "        nll = 0.0\n",
        "        for i in range(len(rates) - 1):\n",
        "            r_curr = max(rates[i], 1e-8)\n",
        "            r_next = max(rates[i + 1], 1e-8)\n",
        "\n",
        "            expected_r = r_curr * exp_minus_kappa_dt + theta * (1 - exp_minus_kappa_dt)\n",
        "\n",
        "            c = 2 * kappa / (sigma ** 2 * (1 - exp_minus_kappa_dt) + 1e-10)\n",
        "            variance = (sigma ** 2 / (2 * kappa + 1e-10)) * (1 - exp_minus_kappa_dt) * (r_curr + r_next)\n",
        "            variance = max(variance, 1e-10)\n",
        "\n",
        "            residual = r_next - expected_r\n",
        "            nll += 0.5 * np.log(2 * np.pi * variance) + 0.5 * (residual ** 2) / variance\n",
        "\n",
        "        return nll\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Tighter bounds based on data characteristics\n",
        "    bounds = [\n",
        "        (0.01, 0.5),                                    # κ: 0.01 to 0.5 (5x/year max reversion)\n",
        "        (max(0.001, mean_rate * 0.5), mean_rate * 1.5), # θ: around observed mean\n",
        "        (0.001, std_rate * 0.5)                         # σ: tighter volatility bound\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "\n",
        "    result = minimize(\n",
        "        negative_log_likelihood,\n",
        "        x0=[kappa_init, theta_init, sigma_init],\n",
        "        method='L-BFGS-B',\n",
        "        bounds=bounds,\n",
        "        options={'maxiter': 5000, 'ftol': 1e-10}\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    if verbose:\n",
        "        print('MLE CALIBRATION RESULTS')\n",
        "        print(f'Optimization converged: {result.success}')\n",
        "        print(f'Log-likelihood: {-result.fun:.4f}')\n",
        "        print()\n",
        "        print(f'Calibrated Parameters:')\n",
        "        print(f'  κ (mean reversion speed): {result.x[0]:.6f}')\n",
        "        print(f'  θ (long-term mean): {result.x[1]:.6f}')\n",
        "        print(f'  σ (volatility): {result.x[2]:.6f}')\n",
        "        print()\n",
        "        feller_lhs = 2 * result.x[0] * result.x[1]\n",
        "        feller_rhs = result.x[2] ** 2\n",
        "        print(f'Feller Condition: 2κθ = {feller_lhs:.6f} >= σ² = {feller_rhs:.6f}?')\n",
        "        print(f'  Status: {\"SATISFIED\" if feller_lhs >= feller_rhs else \"VIOLATED\"}')\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        'kappa': result.x[0],\n",
        "        'theta': result.x[1],\n",
        "        'sigma': result.x[2],\n",
        "        'converged': result.success,\n",
        "        'nll': -result.fun\n",
        "    }\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "jp-MarkdownHeadingCollapsed": true,
        "id": "CIV7wzVnQqvb"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 2.3: OLS Calibration (Fallback)\n",
        "\n",
        "OLS provides a robust alternative if MLE optimization fails."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "2_6YcgJxQqvb",
        "outputId": "f475f30d-7047-4ae4-98b2-c8b813250635"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "OLS calibration function defined\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def ols_calibration(rates, dt, verbose=True):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Calibrate CIR model using Ordinary Least Squares (fallback method)\n",
        "\n",
        "    Based on Vasicek-like linearization: dr_t ≈ α + β*r_t + ε_t\n",
        "    where α = κ*θ*dt, β = 1 - κ*dt\n",
        "\n",
        "    Manual OLS without sklearn dependency.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Calculate changes\n",
        "    dr = np.diff(rates)\n",
        "    X = rates[:-1]  # Current rates\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Minimize sum((dr - α - β*X)^2)\n",
        "    n = len(X)\n",
        "    X_design = np.column_stack([np.ones(n), X])  # Add intercept\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Normal equations: (X^T X)^-1 X^T y\n",
        "    XtX = X_design.T @ X_design\n",
        "    Xty = X_design.T @ dr\n",
        "    coeffs = np.linalg.solve(XtX, Xty)\n",
        "\n",
        "    alpha, beta = coeffs[0], coeffs[1]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Extract CIR parameters\n",
        "    kappa_ols = -beta / dt\n",
        "    theta_ols = alpha / (kappa_ols * dt) if kappa_ols != 0 else np.mean(rates)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Calculate residuals and R²\n",
        "    y_pred = X_design @ coeffs\n",
        "    ss_res = np.sum((dr - y_pred) ** 2)\n",
        "    ss_tot = np.sum((dr - np.mean(dr)) ** 2)\n",
        "    r_squared = 1 - (ss_res / ss_tot) if ss_tot != 0 else 0\n",
        "    residuals = dr - y_pred\n",
        "    sigma_ols = np.std(residuals) / np.sqrt(dt * np.mean(rates))\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Ensure positivity constraints\n",
        "    kappa_ols = max(kappa_ols, 0.01)\n",
        "    theta_ols = max(theta_ols, 0.001)\n",
        "    sigma_ols = max(sigma_ols, 0.001)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if verbose:\n",
        "        print('OLS CALIBRATION RESULTS')\n",
        "        print(f'Regression R²: {r_squared:.6f}')\n",
        "        print()\n",
        "        print(f'Calibrated Parameters:')\n",
        "        print(f'  κ (mean reversion speed): {kappa_ols:.6f}')\n",
        "        print(f'  θ (long-term mean): {theta_ols:.6f}')\n",
        "        print(f'  σ (volatility): {sigma_ols:.6f}')\n",
        "        print()\n",
        "        print(f'Feller Condition: 2κθ = {2*kappa_ols*theta_ols:.6f} >= σ² = {sigma_ols**2:.6f}?')\n",
        "        print(f'  Status: {\"SATISFIED\" if 2*kappa_ols*theta_ols >= sigma_ols**2 else \"VIOLATED\"}')\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        'kappa': kappa_ols,\n",
        "        'theta': theta_ols,\n",
        "        'sigma': sigma_ols,\n",
        "        'r_squared': r_squared,\n",
        "        'converged': True\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"OLS calibration function defined\")\n"
      ]
    },
