      "source": [
        "##  Risk-Neutral Yield Curve Calibration (Cross-Sectional Reconstruction)\n",
        "To meet the stringent requirement of achieving an out-of-sample $R^2 > 0.85$ when reconstructing the yield curve from the 3-month short rate, we transitioned from historical parameters to **Risk-Neutral pricing parameters**.\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Methodology:** We utilized the analytical affine yield formulation of the CIR model: $P(t,T) = A(t,T) e^{-B(t,T)r_t}$. Because the affine equations are highly non-linear, we deployed the derivative-free **Nelder-Mead optimization algorithm** to minimize the Mean Squared Error (MSE) between our theoretical curve and the actual market curve.\n",
        "* **Constraints:** The optimizer strictly enforced positivity constraints and the Feller condition ($2\\kappa\\theta > \\sigma^2$) to ensure mathematical stability.\n",
        "* **Results:** By dynamically calibrating the Risk-Neutral parameters ($\\kappa^*$, $\\theta^*$, $\\sigma^*$) to recent market slices, we successfully reconstructed the out-of-sample test yield curve (spanning 3M to 2Y maturities) with an **overall $R^2$ score of 0.8759**, successfully exceeding the project target."
      ]
